1
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,350
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,360
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 12=

3
00:00:40,119 --> 00:00:40,859
With you here,

4
00:00:42,219 --> 00:00:42,960
somehow,

5
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,039
I'm not as panicked anymore.

6
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:05,560
(Wards / OR)

7
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:37,719
It's okay.

8
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:56,040
Ms. Wen's family!

9
00:02:05,219 --> 00:02:05,760
Here.

10
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:07,459
How's my mom?

11
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:08,900
Her vital signs are stable.

12
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,319
She can be moved to a regular ward.

13
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,379
Go do the paperwork.

14
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:16,780
I'll do it.

15
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,259
Didn't Dr. Pei

16
00:02:23,259 --> 00:02:24,680
finish operating late last night?

17
00:02:24,919 --> 00:02:26,080
Low blood sugar too, I hear?

18
00:02:26,719 --> 00:02:28,080
It's already six in the morning,

19
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,840
and you're still here at the ICU.

20
00:02:30,219 --> 00:02:32,620
You really care about my patient.

21
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:33,960
Don't you have work, Dr. Chen?

22
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:39,880
(ICU)

23
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,520
Have some porridge first.

24
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,360
Your mom's moving wards.

25
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,919
You need to care for her.

26
00:02:49,659 --> 00:02:50,520
You just

27
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:53,060
went to get me porridge?

28
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,500
The cafeteria just opened.

29
00:02:57,099 --> 00:02:58,099
Eat it before it gets cold.

30
00:02:58,219 --> 00:02:59,219
I'll do the paperwork.

31
00:02:59,539 --> 00:03:00,300
Be right back.

32
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,060
(Hot Water / Restroom / Wards / OR)

33
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,660
(Care)

34
00:03:48,539 --> 00:03:49,280
What's wrong?

35
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,400
Why didn't you tell me?

36
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:54,340
If my brother hadn't told me,

37
00:03:54,639 --> 00:03:57,860
I wouldn't know about
my godmother's accident.

38
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,759
All right.

39
00:04:01,139 --> 00:04:02,960
I was in such a rush last night.

40
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,680
She only left the ICU this morning.

41
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,099
I haven't had a chance to tell you.

42
00:04:07,379 --> 00:04:07,759
Come on.

43
00:04:07,939 --> 00:04:09,080
Let me look at you.

44
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,280
How's she doing?

45
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,919
She's fine.

46
00:04:16,459 --> 00:04:18,040
The doctor says she's recovering well.

47
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:20,060
She'll be discharged soon.

48
00:04:21,699 --> 00:04:22,300
Good.

49
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:24,040
Let's take turns.

50
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:25,600
I'll take the days.

51
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,540
You go home and rest.

52
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:27,459
You take the nights.

53
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:28,680
I'll sleep at home.

54
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,980
We can share the load.

55
00:04:37,399 --> 00:04:38,040
Mumu.

56
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,300
It's so good to have you.

57
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,399
Don't get all mushy.

58
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,259
That's what friends are for.

59
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,199
Besides,

60
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,439
she's not just your mom.

61
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,480
She's mine too.

62
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,079
All right.

63
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:00,620
Enough of that.

64
00:05:02,259 --> 00:05:03,899
You've been up all night.

65
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,660
What matters now

66
00:05:07,259 --> 00:05:08,560
is that you get some sleep.

67
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:10,279
I'll stay with her.

68
00:05:11,819 --> 00:05:12,160
Okay.

69
00:05:31,959 --> 00:05:33,199
Get some sleep.

70
00:05:33,879 --> 00:05:34,480
I'm off.

71
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:16,220
Here.

72
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:18,720
Is it good?

73
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:20,860
Try one.

74
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:24,879
Sweet.

75
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,519
Really sweet.

76
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,500
I bought them today.

77
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,180
I'm good.

78
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:30,519
One more.

79
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,420
Ma'am.

80
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:38,000
Awake?

81
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:39,879
Oh, Dr. Pei.

82
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,360
You look much better today.

83
00:06:43,259 --> 00:06:43,819
I feel okay.

84
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:45,439
With a few more days of rest,

85
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:47,240
you should be just about back to normal.

86
00:06:49,899 --> 00:06:50,680
Has my sister left?

87
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:52,980
Just now.

88
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:53,980
She'll come tomorrow.

89
00:06:57,639 --> 00:06:59,879
I've arranged some nutritious meals.

90
00:07:00,079 --> 00:07:00,540
Then...

91
00:07:00,540 --> 00:07:01,920
Dr. Pei, Xiaoyu's awake.

92
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:02,779
Okay.

93
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,560
I'll go over, then.

94
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:07,300
The girl you told me about?

95
00:07:08,819 --> 00:07:09,600
Yes, that's her.

96
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,180
Let me go with you.

97
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,600
Mom, I'll be right back.

98
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,420
Here's your fruit.

99
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,300
Go ahead.

100
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,040
Let's go.

101
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,959
(Wards)

102
00:07:25,959 --> 00:07:26,839
Xiaoyu.

103
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,860
Dr. Pei!

104
00:07:32,019 --> 00:07:33,699
You're awake. Does it hurt?

105
00:07:38,639 --> 00:07:40,259
A little.

106
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:41,740
Just hang in there a little longer.

107
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,040
You can have yummy food tomorrow.

108
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:45,199
Really?

109
00:07:45,199 --> 00:07:46,839
I want strawberries.

110
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:47,959
Okay.

111
00:07:48,279 --> 00:07:49,540
I'll bring you some tomorrow.

112
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:52,759
Dr. Pei.

113
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,459
Dr. Pei.

114
00:07:57,579 --> 00:07:58,379
Without you,

115
00:07:58,939 --> 00:08:00,160
my little girl

116
00:08:00,399 --> 00:08:01,759
wouldn't have made it.

117
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,279
It's my job.

118
00:08:03,939 --> 00:08:04,740
No need to thank me.

119
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:06,639
Dr. Pei.

120
00:08:08,879 --> 00:08:09,600
Today,

121
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,420
I went to find the contractor.

122
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:12,500
But he ran off.

123
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,560
I can't reach him either.

124
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,839
The developer says
it's none of his business.

125
00:08:17,399 --> 00:08:18,000
Dr. Pei.

126
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:19,839
How much more

127
00:08:20,439 --> 00:08:21,980
will her treatment cost?

128
00:08:22,819 --> 00:08:25,519
I really don't have much money left.

129
00:08:25,579 --> 00:08:26,860
Could you...

130
00:08:27,399 --> 00:08:28,040
Dr. Pei.

131
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,339
I'm really short on money.

132
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,319
Sir.

133
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,240
I'm a lawyer.

134
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:34,440
For this case,

135
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,539
I can help you with legal aid.

136
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:02,040
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
